## Why This Is Asked
Tests spanning multi-tenant boundaries and asynchronous export flows surface data isolation and resilience issues. This question probes end-to-end coverage for real-world SaaS data export use cases like Airbnb and Microsoft enterprise products.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant data isolation across services
- Async background jobs and eventual consistency
- End-to-end validation of blob storage and email delivery
- Idempotent retries and fault injection
- Test data strategy and environment isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example test outline (Playwright + API stubs)
test('tenant-scoped data export end-to-end', async ({ page, api, storage }) => {
  await loginAsAdmin(page);
  await page.click('#start-export');
  await page.waitForResponse(r => r.url.includes('/exports/').and(r.status() === 200));
  const status = await api.get(`/exports/${tenantId}/status`);
  expect(status).toHaveProperty('state', 'COMPLETED');
  const blob = await storage.getBlob(`exports/${tenantId}/data.json`);
  expect(blob).toContain(`"tenantId":"${tenantId}"`);
  // idempotence
  await page.click('#start-export');
  const status2 = await api.get(`/exports/${tenantId}/status`);
  expect(status2).toHaveProperty('state', 'COMPLETED');
});
```

